=====================================

**SQL solutions**

---

## Top Performers by Department
Employees with rating = 5 in the most recent year.

```sql
SELECT e.name, d.dept_name
FROM Employees e
JOIN Departments d ON e.dept_id = d.dept_id
JOIN Performance p ON e.emp_id = p.emp_id
WHERE p.year = (SELECT MAX(year) FROM Performance)
  AND p.rating = 5;
```

---

## Average Salary by Department
Average salary per department, sorted descending.

```sql
SELECT d.dept_name, AVG(e.salary) AS avg_salary
FROM Employees e
JOIN Departments d ON e.dept_id = d.dept_id
GROUP BY d.dept_name
ORDER BY avg_salary DESC;
```

---

## Longest Serving Employee
Employee with earliest hire date.

```sql
SELECT name, hire_date
FROM Employees
ORDER BY hire_date ASC
LIMIT 1;
```

---

## Performance-Based Salary Adjustment
Employees with average rating < 3.

```sql
SELECT e.name, e.salary
FROM Employees e
JOIN Performance p ON e.emp_id = p.emp_id
GROUP BY e.emp_id, e.name, e.salary
HAVING AVG(p.rating) < 3;
```